# Deliberately NOT ignored: branch_structure.json, temp_auto_push.bat and
# temp_interactive_push.bat. Those three entries arrived in the same merge
# (1112a18, 1 Aug 2026) that planted the disguised payload, and ignoring them
# is not protection — it is the opposite. An ignored file never shows up in
# `git status`, so a dropped auto-push script would sit in the working tree
# unseen. If any of these names reappears, git must shout about it.

# ─── Editor and agent state — never commit, never push ────────────────────
#
# Per-machine, per-person, and an execution vector: a planted
# `.vscode/tasks.json` with `runOn: folderOpen`, paired with
# `task.allowAutomaticTasks: true` in settings.json, runs a command the moment
# the folder is opened — with no prompt and the terminal hidden. That is
# exactly how a disguised payload was armed in this project on 15 Aug 2026.
# See docs/SECURITY-INCIDENT-2026-08-27.md in bienify-app.
#
# `.gitignore` itself was listed here by merge 31cd87e (31 Aug 2026), which in
# the same change deleted `.vscode/` and the line above naming `runOn:
# folderOpen`. A self-ignoring .gitignore lets these rules be edited without
# the edit showing. Both are restored; neither goes back.
.vscode/
.claude/
